      "subject_newsroom_count": 30,
      "summary": "Canada announced a package of retaliatory tariffs on about $20 billion worth of U.S. goods, with rates applied dollar-for-dollar and reaching as high as 50% on selected items, as part of an escalating trade dispute between the two countries. The measures were framed as direct retaliation for recent U.S. tariffs and are targeted at a wide range of American exports. Coverage across the articles consistently emphasizes the size of the tariff list, the top rate of 50%, and that the action is a response to U.S. trade measures.",
      "takeaway": "Canada has launched a major, proportionate tariff retaliation against U.S. goods in an escalating trade dispute.",
      "why_it_matters": "The tariffs directly affect exporters and importers on both sides, altering costs and trade flows for industries tied to the goods targeted by the measures."
